  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I'm sorry the churros were missing. Unfortunately, I can't compensate for them.\n\n**Order #6103, Taqueria Luz:** The delivery log shows it was handed to you on Wednesday, October 21 at 7:10 PM. Missing or wrong items have to be reported within 48 hours of delivery, which for this order was Friday at 7:10 PM. It's now been about 72 hours, so this is past the reporting window and I'm not able to refund or credit the churros.\n\nI know that's frustrating after the week you've had. If you notice a problem with a future order, reporting it within 48 hours means we can sort it out.\n\nIs there another order you'd like me to look at?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Ugh, that's frustrating, but I'll take it. Why is it 48 hours though? I didn't even notice the churros were missing until the next day, so it's not like I could have reported it sooner."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "That's a fair question, and I understand why it's frustrating. The 48-hour window exists so that item problems get reported while the order is still recent. That way the issue can be checked against the order details and passed on to the restaurant while it's still useful to them. The window applies the same way to every order, and I don't have a way to make exceptions.\n\nYou still had time, though. If you noticed the missing churros the next day, Thursday, you had until Friday evening at 7:10 PM to report them. The window counts from delivery, so noticing a day late still leaves a full day to get in touch. I know that doesn't help with this order, but it's worth knowing for next time. Reporting through the app or chat as soon as you notice something is the safest way to make sure it's covered.\n\nDo you want to go through today's Pho Real order (#6104) or anything else?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, I get it. I'll remember to report things faster. Yes, next is today's lunch from Pho Real, #6104. The iced coffee was missing from it."
